                                    ------
                                    Other Usage
                                    ------
                                    Jay Liang
                                    ------
                                     2007/08/14

More Examples:                                     
	
	You can controls the max number of items to be kept in a rss feed with the appender. For example, 
if you only want 10 items in the feed: 

+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

  Rss20Appender a = new Rss20Appender("text.xml");
  a.setNumItemToKeep(10);
    
  //if there are more than 10 items in 'text.xml' after this item is added,
  //the appender will remove items from the beginning of the feed and keep the last 10 items
  a.addItem(new Item()); 
    
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+


	Static method for reading feed(s):

+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

  File f1 = new File("f1.xml"));
  File f2 = new File("f2.xml"));
  File f3 = new File("f3.xml"));
  List<Channel> channels = Rss20Utils.readAll(f1, f2, f3);
    
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

	Parse an XML string:

+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

  Document doc = XMLUtils.parseXml("<tag></tag>", false, false);
  Element element = XMLUtils.parseXml("<tag></tag>", false, false).getDocumentElement();
    
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
	
	  For more details, I encourage to take a look at the {{{apidocs/index.html}Javadoc}}.
  Also check out the {{{faq.html}FAQ}} section for more insights about this API. 